feat(order): the trade state machine joins — 16 RPCs across the order and its line items

OrderService (9 RPCs) and OrderItemService (7) over the two golden-DDL
tables (the 24-column order — the four amount fields, the recipient
triple, the groupon links, the idempotency/business-ref keys — and the
items with the sku_snapshot jsonb). The lifecycle is the only write
path for status: Create lands as PENDING_PAYMENT, CancelOrder walks
PENDING_PAYMENT to CANCELLED, ConfirmReceipt walks PAID/FULFILLED to
FULFILLED, ExpireOrderByTimeout sweeps a stale pending row (the
Asynq task's face — the task_id/trace_id ride for idempotency), and
the transition helper refuses any move off a non-matching state with
FailedPrecondition. Terminal states never move again.

The status enum maps both ways between the proto values and the bare
member-name spellings the reference's demo data stores (CANCELLED,
PENDING_PAYMENT, ...).

Known gap (the sku drop recorded its first case): the colon-verb
routes (`{id}:cancel`, `{id}:confirm-receipt`, `{id}:adjust-stock`)
answer 405 at the axum 0.8 mount — the gen-http route table carries
the Go-style verb spelling but the adapter's method routing does not
reach it; the framework side is the follow-up. The state machine
itself verified live over the gRPC face: cancel lands CANCELLED, and
the second cancel answers FailedPrecondition with the exact guard
message.

verified: app create order (gated) lands PENDING_PAYMENT; the grpcurl
matrix — cancel, get reads CANCELLED, double-cancel refused — green
